<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bartle Frere</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1815–1884</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sir Henry Bartle Frere, Henry Bartle Frere, Sir Bartle Frere</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Bartle Frere was a British colonial administrator. After a career in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, where he was Governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Bombay</a>, he led a mission to Zanzibar in 1873 that pressed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Barghash to sign a treaty ending the seaborne <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a>. As High Commissioner for Southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> from 1877 he provoked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-zulu-war">Anglo-Zulu War</a> of 1879 and was recalled.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bartle-frere.jpg" alt="Bartle Frere" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Reid · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_(Henry)_Bartle_Frere,_1st_Bt_by_Sir_George_Reid.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
